<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 69 0 R/T(What Should Hearing Aids Cost in Australia?)/E(What Should Hearing Aids Cost in Australia?)/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

196 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(More than 3.6 million Australians are estimated to have some level of hearing loss, yet one of the most confusing parts of buying hearing aids is still the price. Depending on the technology and provider, a pair can cost anywhere from a few thousand dollars to close to $10,000 or more.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

197 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(That naturally raises an important question: what are you actually paying for?)/Pg 15 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

198 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 69 0 R/T(Why do prices vary so much?)/E(Why do prices vary so much?)/Pg 15 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

199 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(Part of the difference comes down to the hearing aid itself. Higher technology levels generally include more sophisticated sound processing, greater support in difficult listening environments and additional features such as automation, personalisation and connectivity.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

200 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(But the device is only part of the overall cost. Depending on the provider, your purchase may also include hearing assessments, professional fitting and programming, follow-up appointments, fine-tuning, ongoing clinical support, warranty, trial periods and accessories. This is why two quotes can look very different even when the devices themselves appear similar.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

201 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 69 0 R/T(More expensive does not automatically mean better)/E(More expensive does not automatically mean better)/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

202 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(A premium hearing aid may be worthwhile for someone who regularly needs to follow conversations in restaurants, meetings and busy social environments. Someone with simpler listening needs may get far less benefit from paying thousands more for technology they rarely use.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

203 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(The goal is not to buy the cheapest hearing aid or the most expensive one. It is to pay for the technology you will actually use.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

204 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(PRICING)/Pg 15 0 R/K[10]>>
